CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 8
Women and Children victims of acts of Violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
f. the right to restitution;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to obtain facilities in the judicial process; and/or j. the right to assistance.

Article 1 I
A child as a victim of an act, in addition to receiving the rights of Violence as referred to in Article 8, also receives special rights, as follows:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development; b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or
e. the right to obtain freedom.

Article 24
(1) The provision of services to victims as referred to in Article 17 shall be implemented with:
a. every day (including holidays);
b. promptly;
c. safe and comfortable;
d. a sense of empathy;
e. non-discrimination;
f. outreach;
g. free of charge; and
h. guaranteed confidentiality.
(2) Service providers or service managers are prohibited from collecting any fees from victims of violence.

